, and burn it upon the altar.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¹And he shall do with the bullock as he did with the bullock for a sin offering, so shall he do with this: and the priest shall make an atonement for them, and it shall be forgiven them.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙAnd he shall carry forth the bullock without the camp, and burn him as he burned the first bullock: it is a sin offering for the congregation.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¬When a ruler hath sinned, and done somewhat through ignorance against any of the commandments of the LORD his God concerning things which should not be done, and is guilty;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ†or if his sin, wherein he hath sinned, come to his knowledge; he shall bring his offering, a kid of the goats, a male without blemish:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ—and he shall lay his hand upon the head of the goat, and kill it in the place where they kill the burnt offering before the LORD: it is a sin offering.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙĞAnd the priest shall take of the blood of the sin offering with his finger, and put it upon the horns of the altar of burnt offering, and shall pour out his blood at the bottom of the altar of burnt offering.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÁAnd he shall burn all his fat upon the altar, as the fat of the sacrifice of peace offerings: and the priest shall make an atonement for him as concerning his sin, and it shall be forgiven him.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ»And if any one of the common people sin through ignorance, while he doeth somewhat against any of the commandments of the LORD concerning things which ought not to be done, and be guilty;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ­or if his sin, which he hath sinned, come to his knowledge: then he shall bring his offering, a kid of the goats, a female without blemish, for his sin which he hath sinned.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙzAnd he shall lay his hand upon the head of the sin offering, and slay the sin offering in the place of the burnt offering.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¾And the priest shall take of the blood thereof with his finger, and put it upon the horns of the altar of burnt offering, and shall pour out all the blood thereof at the bottom of the altar.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÚAnd he shall take away all the fat thereof, as the fat is taken away from off the sacrifice of peace offerings; and the priest shall burn it upon the altar for a sweet savour unto the LORD; and the priest shall make an atonement for him, and it shall be forgiven him.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verse ªlast_verse#¦verses”„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙVAnd if he bring a lamb for a sin offering, he shall bring it a female without blemish.¦layout ªlast_verse „¥verse!¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙŒAnd he shall lay his hand upon the head of the sin offering, and slay it for a sin offering in the place where they kill the burnt offering.¦layout ªlast_verse!„¥verse"¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÊAnd the priest shall take of the blood of the sin offering with his finger, and put it upon the horns of the altar of burnt offering, and shall pour out all the blood thereof at the bottom of the altar:¦layout ªlast_verse"„¥verse#¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÚJand he shall take away all the fat thereof, as the fat of the lamb is taken away from the sacrifice of the peace offerings; and the priest shall burn them upon the altar, according to the offerings made by fire unto the LORD: and the priest shall make an atonement for his sin that he hath committed, and it sh